        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 659,
            "text": "What is your goal? Creating invoices in an external system with REST API based on CRM data from Airtable. What is the problem & what have you tried? I cannot map array data for dynamic amount of invoice rows to the HTTP POST module’s “invoice rows” section. I have tried without “Map” on, but then I can only see one of the values, and I cannot figure out how to do with “Map” on. I guess a basic question is if I even should be able to map the values directly to the HTTP POST module, or if I would need to some other “re-packaging” module before that? For some reason I cannot upload more than one screenshot, so I chose the mapping view with “Map” enabled.",
            "sha256": "4077a293d7ff9913f581e260dc76d71e9256904c670a4ccc6fe5a25f2e2fcd13"
          },
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 688,
            "end": 1043,
            "text": "Error messages or input/output bundles Example of Airtable’s “Get Record” output data, where two values exist: { “Bundle 1”: { “Hinta 0% (from Ostettu tuote)”: [ 390.4382470119522, 79.6812749003984 ], “VAT rate (from Ostettu tuote)”: [ 0.255, 0.255 ], “Hinta 25.5% (from Ostettu tuote)”: [ 490, 100 ] } Screenshots (scenario flow, module settings, errors)",
